Original commit body from 2d85f730d5dcceddd9f092fb60836ed87942452a:

WI-bifob, per owner ruling 2026-08-03. A taint-flow verdict is a
DISJUNCTION over its flows, so one flow from test code held an entire
claim at `violated` and no precision work elsewhere could move it.

Measured on the 9-repo cohort: 2 of 18 violated claims rested entirely
on a single test-sourced flow each -- pretix/host-secret-no-network on a
tests/e2e/conftest.py reading an env var into urlopen, and
alertmanager/untrusted-input-no-network on a tls_transport_test.go
dialling TLS. Neither is a statement about the shipped product.

Flows whose SOURCE is test, fixture or migration code are now excluded
from taint-claim verdicts. Classification is on the source side, where
data enters: a test reaching a real network primitive is still a test
doing its job, and a production function reaching a primitive inside a
test helper is still a production flow.

- Exclusions are DISCLOSED, never dropped. Each verdict carries an
  `excluded_flows` bucket keyed by reason, reported on confirmed
  verdicts as well as violated ones -- that is where a silent filter
  misleads most, since the claim reads clean and the reader cannot tell
  flows existed. D7 shape: a production default plus labelled buckets.
- --include-non-production-sources restores the previous behavior, so
  this is a default rather than a filter.
- paths.is_migration_file is new and deliberately NOT folded into
  is_test_file: a migration is production code that ships and runs once
  at deploy, not test scaffolding. Declared scope, with `versions/`
  claimed only under alembic/ and migrate|migration only under db/ --
  claiming words that common outright would silently drop real
  production flows from a security verdict. Measured need: is_test_file
  caught 84 of the 98 non-production rows and missed exactly the 14
  Django migrations.
- The id path slot is parsed RIGHT-ANCHORED, since it is the one
  colon-tolerant slot in the grammar (ADR-0036 D1a). Rather than add a
  seventh naive copy, this one is correct and pinned by a test; the six
  existing homes and the two defective ones are filed as WI-ribuz,
  WI-guror, WI-nukas, WI-dosir.

Envelope schema 1.1 -> 1.2, additive. Spec updated with the new default
and the schema bump; CLI flag-matrix baseline regenerated.

Measured against a prediction registered before the run. Which claims
flip and how many: exactly as predicted, no wrong-direction flips.
Volume was predicted in the WRONG UNIT and is recorded as such: evidence
rows fell 354 -> 270 (-84) while the underlying exclusions were 692
flow-claim pairs (675 test, 17 migration). The gap is the evidence cap
-- pretix/untrusted-input-no-database went 748 -> 140 flows (-81%) yet
still displays 100 rows, because removing flows from an over-cap claim
changes WHICH rows are shown rather than how many.

Scope-axis caveat: this is not a cohort-wide property. 74 of the 98
non-production rows are caddy, 64 of them from a single file.

